    "max_theorem1_residual": 7.771561172376096e-16,
    "scientific_verdict": "Across prime-power moduli q = p^r (q = 9, 27) and k in {2, 3} oracle calls, averaging the k-call Born distribution over the p-adic secret subgroup H_j = p^{r-j} Z_{p^r}^n pinches the trajectory sum onto the congruence collision variety V_epsilon^{(j)}(f) = {(w, w') : tau_epsilon(w) == tau_epsilon(w') mod p^j}. The varieties form a monotone filtration whose successive valuation shells D_epsilon^{(j)}(f) = V_epsilon^{(j)}(f) \\ V_epsilon^{(j+1)}(f) contain zero diagonal pairs, have zero-sum oscillatory probability increments across x in {0, ..., D-1}, and telescope exactly to the full gap between single-instance and uniform-secret averages."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
